&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord is used by over 200 million people every month for many different reasons, but there’s one thing that nearly everyone does on our platform:&lt;strong&gt; play video games.&lt;/strong&gt; Over 90% of our users play games, spending a combined 1.5 billion hours playing thousands of unique titles on Discord each month. Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to talk and hang out before, during, and after playing games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: This is a temporary, full-time position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workday plays a central role in managing our people&#39;s data, connecting with numerous internal applications and a wide array of external systems. It serves as the quiet hub, facilitating an exchange of information to keep everything in sync across our organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team as a Senior Integrations Analyst, and play a pivotal role in shaping the connectivity landscape between Workday and our internal systems. Whether you&#39;re based in San Francisco or working remotely, your expertise will drive the seamless integration that powers our success. The ideal candidate will question common assumptions, rethink existing design, configurations, and see every challenge as an opportunity for system improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our People Systems Team innovates and streamlines how we manage our most valuable asset—our people. This committed, multi-talented team shapes and optimizes systems that support the entire employee lifecycle. From recruitment and onboarding to performance management and beyond, the People Systems Team uses cutting-edge technology and a deep understanding of organizational needs to foster talent. The People Systems Team leads the way in creating a culture that values people and performance by working together, thinking forward, and fostering excellence.&amp;nbsp;This role will report to the Senior Director of People Technology &amp;amp; Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the subject matter expert on large collections of Workday integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and implement complex integrations between Workday and various external/internal systems using Workday Integration Tools (EIB, Core Connectors, Studio, Cloud Connect, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain integrations that support data flows, ensuring accurate and efficient communication between Workday &amp;amp; internal/external systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with business stakeholders and other internal teams to understand integration requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into technical specifications and design documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct unit testing, integration testing, and end-to-end testing for developed integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve production-related integration issues in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain comprehensive documentation for integrations, including design documents, process flows, and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that integrations comply with security and data privacy standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with security teams to implement and maintain security best practices for integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other teams, business analysts, and stakeholders to understand overall business objectives and ensure that integrations align with organizational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with Workday releases and updates, and assess their impact on existing integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement enhancements to existing integrations, as needed, including annual events such as open enrollment &amp;amp; compensation events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 6+ years of experience as a Workday Integration Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Workday Integration tools and technologies such as Workday Studio, Workday Payroll Interfaces, &amp;amp; Workday’s connector library, with expertise in building and maintaining RESTful and SOAP based API integrations using OAuth2.0 authentication flows and certificate based security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced skills in XSLT transformations, JSON manipulation and XML schema design and data mapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with iPaaS platforms, particularly Workato, including recipe development and custom connectors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of Workday&#39;s data model, business processes, and security features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in integrating across business systems beyond the People &amp;amp; Talent team, such as Finance, Corporate Engineering, and IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with various integration patterns, protocols, and data formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Workday administrative functions including tenant configuration, data loads, payroll configurations and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developing Workday custom reports and calculated fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working in a fast-paced environment with stakeholders and users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday Extend Experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday Integration Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday Studio Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;US Remote:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position is temporary, US-based, and can be remote, but if you live in the Bay Area, you’re welcome to work from our beautiful SF office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;The US base salary range for this &lt;strong&gt;temporary&lt;/strong&gt; full-time position is &lt;strong&gt;$192,000&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to &lt;strong&gt;$216,000, prorated based on tenure + benefits. &lt;/strong&gt;Our salary ranges are determined by role and level. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include benefits.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Discord?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We&#39;re a multiplatform, multigenerational and multiplayer platform that helps people deepen their friendships around games and shared interests. We believe games give us a way to have fun with our favorite people, whether listening to music together or grinding in competitive matches for diamond rank. &lt;strong&gt;Join us in our mission! Your future is just a click away!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discord is committed to inclusion and providing reasonable accommodations during the interview process. &lt;/strong&gt;We want you to feel set up for success, so if you are in need of reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please see our Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy for details regarding Discord’s collection and usage of personal information relating to the application and recruitment process by clicking&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://discord.com/terms/applicant-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;HERE.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
